hey everyone I'm Abby sharp welcome to  Abby's kitchen if you haven't heard 2016  was recently named the international  year of the pulse and no I'm not talking  about your heartbeat that's something  you want to celebrate every year but  pulses actually include all your dried  peas chickpeas beans and lentils and  their nutritional powerhouse is packed  with fiber and protein and if the first  thing you think about when you hear the  word beans is the magic fruit the more  you eat the more you  well actually guys it's not true more  eat the less you're gonna - so eat up  we are seeing pulses appear on  restaurant menus all over the world even  celebrity chefs are finding ways to  incorporate pulses into their recipes so  to celebrate the year of the pulse  thousands of people all over the world  are taking the pulse pledge promising to  enjoy pulses at least once a day for 10  weeks straight thankfully I've parted up  with my favorite pulse ox knack Sabra  hummus to bring you some of the easiest  ways to meet your pulse target let's get  started  tip 1 make black bean soup in a flash I  heat a few cans of black beans with  jarred salsa the vegetable broth chili  powder and cumin  then I puree it into a smooth soup and  serve it top with avocado  plain Greek yogurt and cilantro tip -  paca hummus snack pack a container of  Saveur hummus and whole-grain crackers  for your purse  office desk or gym bag the combination  of fiber protein and carbs is going to  help you get through any workout or that  3p an energy depth tip 3 upgrade your  avocado toast with white beans add  protein to this trendy breakfast by  pureeing a can of white beans with  avocado lemon juice parsley basil garlic  and oil and smearing on whole grain  toast tip 4 bring fiber and protein to  your cookout with hummus burgers mix  together a quarter cup of sauteed onions  with 1 pound of lean ground beef and a  quarter cup of roasted red pepper Sabra  hummus form into patties grill until  cooked through and serve on whole grain  buns smeared with a little more hummus  tip five boost protein in your Bolognese  just add a can of cooked lentils to your  favorite pasta sauce and serve it on a  bed of spaghetti how do you plan to take  the pulse pledge leave me a message  below or tweet some your favorite  recipes to me using the hashtag pulse  pledge thank you so much for watching  more great meal and snack ideas be sure  to subscribe to my channel and I'll see  you next time on Abbey's kitchen
 

